module

public import AFree.Curves.BundleTop.Main

/-!
# `V = ℝ^d` almost everywhere implies absolute continuity

If the decomposability bundle of a finite measure `μ` equals `ℝ^d` at `μ`-a.e. point, then
`μ ≪ 𝓛^d`. A countable dense family of axes `wᵢ` and apertures `1/(n+2)` yields cone-null sets;
the span `W(x)` of their limit directions is a Borel subspace field passing the `C¹`-arc test, so it
contains the bundle, and `d` independent cones give absolute continuity through curve currents.
-/
